===Glyph origin===
Originates from China, possibly a variant of {{och-l|*澇}}. It appears in the ''{{w|Longkan Shoujian}}'' as being pronounced as {{ltc-l|澇}} or {{ltc-l|勞}}. Often mistaken for a {{ja-r|国字|こくじ}}, the {{ja-r|ゆり}} and {{ja-r|しなたり}} readings are instead an instance of {{ja-r|国訓|こっくん}}.<ref>[https://dl.ndl.go.jp/pid/2544312/1/28 ''Longkan Shoujian'' in the National Diet Library], book 2, page 26, character 10</ref><ref>{{R:Wasei Kanji 2014|2627}}</ref>

Folk etymology claims that it was coined by {{w|Date Tsunamura}} when he was looking out at the sea through the gate of {{w|大年寺|Dainenji Temple|lang=ja}} in [[Sendai]];<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20240302021704/https://www.city.natori.miyagi.jp/natori100/019.htm 閖上の「閖」の文字] (from official website of Natori City)</ref> however, the character greatly predates him.

